:: Arcade Lock [nobr]
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "arcade">><<effects>><<set $lock to 300>>
The arcade is closed. A glowing sign beside the door reads "Opens: <span class="gold"><<if $timestyle is "ampm">>9:00 am<<else>>9:00<</if>></span>"
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggery gte $lock>>
	<span class="green">The lock looks easy to pick.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Pick it (0:10)|Arcade]]>><<pass 10>><<crimeup 20>><<set $logprep to "Broke into the arcade.">><<log $logprep $lockpickimportance>><<info "locks" "arcade|door" $lock "success">><</link>><<crime>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<span class="red">The lock looks beyond your ability to pick.</span><<skulduggeryrequired>><<info "locks" "arcade|door" $lock "chance">>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Leave|Starfish Street]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcade [nobr]
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "arcade">><<effects>>
<<if $loglocations is 1>><<log "Was at the arcade." $locationimportance>><</if>>
<<set $kylar_play to 0>>
You are in the amusement arcade on Starfish Street.

<<if $daystate is "day" or $daystate is "dusk">>
The games and gambling machines beep and whirr.
<<else>>
The games and gambling machines lie silent.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $stress gte 10000>>
<<passoutarcade>>
<<else>>
	<<if $hour is 21>>
	It's closing time. Security is herding everyone outside.<<if $exposed gte 1>>Panic swells within you as you realise how exposed you'll be should security find you in this state of dress.<</if>>
	<br><br>

		<<if $exposed lte 0>>
		<<link [[Go Outside|Starfish Street]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<else>>
		<<link [[Hide until it's over (1:00)|Arcade]]>><<pass 1 hour>><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>

		<<if $daystate is "night" or $daystate is "dawn">>
		You are alone in the darkness.
		<br><br>
		<<elseif $exposed gte 1>>
		You hide beneath a pinball machine to protect your dignity.
		<br><br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $money gte 500 and ($daystate is "day" or $daystate is "dusk") and $exposed lte 0>>
			<<link [[Play (£5 0:20)|Arcade Play]]>><<set $money -= 500>><<pass 20>><<stress -2>><</link>><<lstress>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $exposed lte 0 and $NPCName[$NPCNameList.indexOf("Kylar")].state is "active" and $weather is "rain" and $daystate is "day">>
			<<if $schoolday isnot 1 or $hour lte 8 or $hour gte 15>>
				<br>
				You see Kylar playing on one of the cabinets.
				<br>
				<<link [[Approach|Kylar Arcade]]>><</link>>
				<br><br>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>

		<<link [[Leave|Starfish Street]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Arcade Play [nobr]
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "arcade">><<effects>>

<<if $leftarm is "bound" and $rightarm is "bound">>
	Playing arcade games with both hands tied behind your back turns out to be <<print either("tricky.","exactly as hard as you'd imagine.","hard. Unsurprisingly.")>>
	<<print either("You lose almost instantly.","In just seconds, your grizzled survivor is zombie food.","In just seconds, your brave soldier is alien food.","In barely a minute, your brave crew are shark meat.")>>
	<<if $rng lte 34>>A few kids nearby witness your crushing defeat. One starts to mimic you, <<print either("gurning","pulling a stupid-face","gazing stupidly")>> over his shoulder at the screen
		while <<print either("trying to reach","flapping at","slapping at")>> the controllers with his hands behind his back.
		<br>
		His cronies find this hilarious.
		<br>
		In fairness, it is possible you look <<print either("kind of dumb","pretty damn stupid","a bit 'special'","pretty fucking mental")>> right now.
		<<lcool>><<status -5>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $money gte 500 and $daystate isnot "night">>
		<<link [[Persist (£5 0:03)|Arcade Play]]>><<set $money -= 500>><<pass 3>><<stress 2>><</link>><<gstress>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Stop|Arcade]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $rng gte 80>>
	You play a shooter, and kill lots of <<print either("zombies", "pirates", "aliens", "soldiers", "criminals", "mutants")>>.
	<<set $logprep to "shooter">>
	<br><br>
	<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
	<<if $danger gte (9900 - $allure) and $eventskip is 0>>
		<<arcadeevent "shooter">>
	<<else>>
		<<set $rng to random(1, 100)>>
		<<if $rng gte 71 - ($gamerskill.shooter/3)>>
			You blow the final boss' head off with a satisfying squelch.
			<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
			<<set $logprep2 to " it went well">>
			<<set $gamerskill.shooter += 1>>
		<<elseif $rng gte 31>>
			You manage to get to that one part of the game everyone complains about. You're reminded why.
			<<set $gamerskill.shooter += 0.5>>
		<<else>>
			You swear the gun isn't working properly. You try to shoot an enemy attack out of the air, but instead take it to the face.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade"+$logprep2+".">>
		<<log $logprep 1>>
		<<endevent "ArcG1" 0>>
		<<arcadeoptions>>
	<</if>>
<<elseif $rng gte 60 and $rng % 2>>
	You play a fighting game.
	<<set $logprep to "fighting">>
	<br><br>
		<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
		<<if $danger gte (9900 - $allure) and $eventskip is 0>>
			<<arcadeevent "fighting">>
		<<else>>
			<<set $rng to random(1, 100)>>
			<<if $rng gte 71 - ($gamerskill.fighting/3)>>
				You beat the final boss with a satisfying punch.
				<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
				<<set $gamerskill.fighting += 1>>
				<<set $logprep2 to " it went well">>
			<<elseif $rng gte 31>>
				You do decently.
				<<set $gamerskill.fighting += 0.5>>
			<<else>>
				You keep failing to pull off combos and lose quickly.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade"+$logprep2+".">>
			<<log $logprep 1>>
			<<endevent "ArcG2" 0>>
			<<arcadeoptions>>
		<</if>>
<<elseif $rng gte 60>>
	You play a beat-em-up game.
	<<set $logprep to "beat-em-up">>
	<br><br>
		<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
		<<if $danger gte (9900 - $allure) and $eventskip is 0>>
			<<arcadeevent "beat-em-up">>
		<<else>>
			<<set $rng to random(1, 100)>>
			<<if $rng gte 71 - ($gamerskill.fighting/3)>>
				You beat the final boss with a satisfying punch.
				<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
				<<set $logprep2 to " it went well">>
			<<elseif $rng gte 31>>
				You get a few stages in but end up losing around the mid point.
			<<else>>
				You get to the final boss but end up losing.
			<</if>>
			<<set $gamerskill.fighting += 0.5>>
			<br><br>
			<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade"+$logprep2+".">>
			<<log $logprep 1>>
			<<endevent "ArcG3" 0>>
			<<arcadeoptions>>
		<</if>>
<<elseif $rng gte 40 and $rng % 2>>
	You play a dancing game.
	<<set $logprep to "dancing">>
	<br><br>
	<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
	<<if $danger gte (9900 - $allure) and $eventskip is 0>>
		<<arcadeevent "dancing">>
	<<else>>
		<<set $rng to random(1, 100)>>
		<<if $danceskill gte $rng*6+400 - $gamerskill.rhythm>>
			You do well.
			<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
			<<danceskilluse>>
			<<set $gamerskill.rhythm += 0.5>>
			<<set $logprep2 to " it went well">>
		<<elseif $danceskill gte $rng*6>>
			It's a little too fast for you, and you barely keep up with the rhythm.
			<<danceskilluse>>
			<<set $gamerskill.rhythm += 0.5>>
		<<else>>
			You make many mistakes and get a bad score.
		<</if>>
		<<tiredness 1>><<physique 1>>
		<br>
		<br>
		<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade"+$logprep2+".">>
		<<log $logprep 1>>
		<<endevent "ArcG4" 0>>
		<<arcadeoptions>>
	<</if>>
<<elseif $rng gte 40>>
	You play a rhythm game.
	<<set $logprep to "rhythm">>
	<br><br>
		<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
		<<if $danger gte (9900 - $allure) and $eventskip is 0>>
			<<arcadeevent "rhythm">>
		<<else>>
			<<set $rng to random(1, 100)>>
			<<if $rng gte 71 - ($gamerskill.rhythm/3)>>
				You nail it and make barely any mistakes.
				<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
				<<set $gamerskill.rhythm += 1>>
				<<set $logprep2 to " it went well">>
			<<elseif $rng gte 31>>
				You struggle a bit and don't get a very good result.
				<<set $gamerskill.rhythm += 0.5>>
			<<else>>
				You can barely keep the rhythm and make many mistakes
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade"+$logprep2+".">>
			<<log $logprep 1>>
			<<endevent "ArcG5" 0>>
			<<arcadeoptions>>
		<</if>>
<<elseif $rng gte 20>>
	You play <<print either("a high speed", "a futuristic", "a surreal", "a colourful", "a realistic")>> racing game.
	<<set $logprep to "racing">>
	<br><br>
		<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
		<<if $danger gte (9900 - $allure) and $eventskip is 0>>
			<<arcadeevent "racing">>
		<<else>>
			<<set $rng to random(1, 100)>>
			<<if $rng gte 71 - ($gamerskill.racing/3)>>
				You race past the competition and during the final lap you even drive past some of the cars in the last places.
				<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
				<<set $gamerskill.racing += 1>>
				<<set $logprep2 to " it went well">>
			<<elseif $rng gte 31>>
				Race starts off decently but you never quite make it to the top spots.
				<<set $gamerskill.racing += 0.5>>
			<<else>>
				You were in the lead for a while, but during the last stretch you make a mistake and cars just behind you finish before you.
				<<set $gamerskill.racing += 0.5>>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade"+$logprep2+".">>
			<<log $logprep 1>>
			<<endevent "ArcG6" 0>>
			<<arcadeoptions>>
		<</if>>
<<elseif $rng gte 10>>
	<<set $logprep to "pinball">>
	You play pinball.
	<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
	<<if $danger gte (9900 - $allure) and $eventskip is 0>>
		<<arcadeevent "pinball">>
	<<else>>
		<<set $rng to random(1, 100)>>
		<<if $rng gte 71 - ($gamerskill.pinball/3)>>
			<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
			<<set $gamerskill.pinball += 1>>
			It goes well.
			<<set $logprep2 to " it went well">>
		<<elseif $rng gte 31>>
			It goes decently.
		<<else>>
			It goes badly.
		<</if>>
		<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade"+$logprep2+".">>
		<<log $logprep 1>>
		<<endevent "ArcG7" 0>>
		<<arcadeoptions>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	You play a fast-paced shmup.
	<<set $logprep to "shmup">>
	<br><br>
	<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
	<<if $danger gte (9900 - $allure) and $eventskip is 0>>
		<<arcadeevent "shmup">>
	<<else>>
		<<set $rng to random(1, 100)>>
		<<if $rng gte 71 - ($gamerskill.shmup/3)>>
			Luck is on your side. The right powerup drops at the right moment, and you blaze through to victory.
			<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
			<<set $logprep2 to " it went well">>
		<<elseif $rng gte 31>>
			It's a little too fast for you, and you're shot down halfway through the game.
		<<else>>
			You almost make it, but the final boss proves too tough.
		<</if>>
		<<set $gamerskill.shmup += 1>>
		<br><br>
		<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade"+$logprep2+".">>
		<<log $logprep 1>>
		<<endevent "ArcG8" 0>>
		<<arcadeoptions>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Arcade Watched Stop [nobr]
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "arcade">><<effects>>

You move away from the <<personstop>> Better safe than sorry.
<br><br>
<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade but a "+$person+" started standing very close to me so I stopped.">>
<<log $logprep 1>>
<<endevent $eventstr>>
<<arcadeoptions>>

:: Arcade Watched Play [nobr]
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "arcade">><<effects>>

<<if $logprep is "beat-em-up">>
	<<set $gamerskill.fighting += 0.5>>
<<elseif $logprep is "dancing">>
	<<set $gamerskill.rhythm += 0.5>>
<<else>>
	<<set $gamerskill[$logprep] += 0.5>>
<</if>>
<<if $rng gte 81>>
You keep playing. The <<person>> creeps closer, until <<he>> presses against your back. <<His>> hands reach out.
<br><br>
<<set $logprep to "While playng a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade I kept playing despite a "+$person+" moving to stand very close to me and then">>
<<link [[Next|Arcade Watched Rape]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>
<br>

<<else>>
You decide you're being paranoid, and keep playing. The <<person>> soon wanders away to offer advice to someone else.
<br><br>
<<set $logprep to "I played a "+$logprep+" game at the arcade but a "+$person+" trying to give me advise started standing way too close to me so I stopped.">>
<<log $logprep 1>>
<<endevent $eventstr>>
<<arcadeoptions>>

<</if>>

:: Arcade Watched Dance [nobr]
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "town">><<effects>>

/* should add chastity, no underwear and crossdressing+no undies reactions */
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<stress 1>><<tiredness 1>><<danceskilluse>><<physique 1>>
	<<set $gamerskill.rhythm += 0.5>>
	You keep playing despite the fact that the <<person>> might be seeing under your skirt.
	<<exhibitionism1>>
	<br>
	<<if $danceskill gte $rng*6+400>>
		You manage to play well despite the situation.
		<br><br>
		<<ltrauma>><<trauma -1>>
		<<if $rng % 4 is 1>> 
			
			<<set $phase to -1>>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade a person stood behind me and crouched down giving "+$him+" a chance to see under my skirt, when I was done">>
		<<else>>
			<<He>> notices another person paying attention to <<him>> and <<he>> quietly moves away before you're done.
			<br><br>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade a person stood behind me and crouched down giving "+$him+" a chance to see under my skirt but I managed to play well despite that.">>
			<<log $logprep 2>>
		<</if>> 
	<<else>>
		<<His>> stare is too distracting and you play badly.
		<<if $rng % 3 is 1>> 
			<<He>> seems to enjoy how concious of <<him>> you seem to be.
			<br><br>
			<<set $phase to -1>>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade a person stood behind me and crouched down giving "+$him+" a chance to see under my skirt distracting me, when I was done">>
		<<else>>
			<<He>> notices it and looks apologetic before moving on.
			<br><br>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade a person stood behind me and crouched down giving "+$him+" a chance to see under my skirt causing me to be distracted and play badly.">>
			<<log $logprep 2>>
		<</if>> 
	<</if>>
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	<<tiredness 2>><<danceskilluse>><<physique 1>><<wearandtear "dance">>
	<<if $worn.lower.skirt is 1>>
		You keep playing and focus on making the movement of your ass and hips as tantalising as possible and giving the <<person>> plenty of chances to see under your skirt.
		<<exhibitionism3>>
		<<set $logprep2 to "seemingly trying to peek under my skirt">>
	<<else>>
		Now with someone watching you decide to put more effort into looking good while you play.
		<<set $logprep2 to "">>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $danceskill gte $rng*6+400>>
		You perform well.
		<<if $rng % 2>> 
			<br><br>
			<<set $phase to -1>>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game someone came by to watch "+$logprep2+" so I decided to show off my skills and body which went well, when I was done">>
		<<else>> 
			<<He>> whistles appreciatively seeming very impressed with your skills but moves on after a while.
			<<stress -2>><<lstress>>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game someone came by to watch "+$logprep2+" so I decided to show off my skills and body, "+$he+" seemed satisfied with my performance.">>
			<<log $logprep 2>>
		<</if>> 
	<<else>>
		Your score suffers and you feel like you ended up looking more <<if !$rng % 2>>silly<<else>><<if $awareness gte 100>>slutty<<else>>desperate<</if>><</if>> than good.
		<<if !$rng % 2>> 
			<<He>> seems to enjoy watching you anyway and when you're done <<he>> gives you a appreciative nod and a smile before moving on.
			<br><br>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade someone came by to watch "+$logprep2+" so I decided to show off my skills and body but I ended up mostly just looking silly but "+$he+" seemed to enjoy watching me despite that.">>
		<<else>>
			<<He>> seems to enjoy watching your antics anyway.
			<br><br>
			<<set $phase to -1>>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade someone came by to watch "+$logprep2+" so I decided to show off my skills and body which went well, when I was done">>
			<<log $logprep 2>>
		<</if>> 
	<</if>>
<<else>>/* no skirt, no show off */
	<<stress 1>><<tiredness 1>><<danceskilluse>><<physique 1>>
	<<set $gamerskill.rhythm += 0.5>>
	You keep playing ignoring the <<person>> watching you.
	<br>
	<<if $danceskill gte $rng*6+400>>
		You nail it and play way better than you were expecting.
		<<if $rng % 5 is 1>> 
			<<He>> seems to enjoy seeing how well you're moving.
			<br><br>
			<<set $phase to -1>>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade someone came by to watch and enjoy seeing how well I was doing, when I was done">>
		<<else>>
			<<He>> seems to get bored and leaves after a while.
			<br><br>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade someone came by to watch but "+$he+" got bored and left despite how well I was doing.">>
			<<log $logprep 2>>
		<</if>> 
	<<else>>
		<<if $rng % 5 is 1>> 
			You don't so well but <<he>> seems to enjoy watching you fail.
			<br><br>
			<<set $phase to -1>>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade someone came by to watch my terrible performance, when I was done">>
		<<else>>
			You don't so well and <<he>> eventually leaves seeming bored.
			<br><br>
			<<set $logprep to "While playing a dancing game at the arcade someone came by and after watching my terrible performance for a bit "+$he+" got bored and left.">>
			<<log $logprep 2>>
		<</if>> 
	<</if>> 
<</if>>
<<if $phase is -1>>
	When you finish <<he>> moves behind you and grabs your ass.
	<<stress 1>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $promiscuity gte 15>>
		<<link [[Allow it|Arcade Watched Sex]]>><</link>><<promiscuous2>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<set $rng to random(1, 100)>>
	<<if $physique gte $rng * 90 + 6000 or $rng is 1>>
		<<link [[Struggle|Arcade Watched Rape]]>>
			<<set $logprep to $he+" grabbed my ass">>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Struggle|Arcade Watched Shove]]>>
			<<set $logprep to $he+" grabbed my ass but I shoved him away.">>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<endevent "ArcE3">>
	<<arcadeoptions>>
<</if>> 

:: Arcade Watched Rape [nobr]

<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<combatstart>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>

	<<maninit>>
	<<set $rescue to 1>>
<</if>>

<<effects>>

<<effectsman>><<man>>

<<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>

<<if $enemyhealth lte 0>>
<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Arcade Watched Rape Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<elseif $enemyarousal gte $enemyarousalmax>>
<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Arcade Watched Rape Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<elseif $alarm is 1 and $rescue is 1>>
<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Arcade Watched Rape Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Arcade Watched Rape]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Arcade Watched Rape Finish [nobr]
<<effects>>
<<if $enemyarousal gte $enemyarousalmax>>
<<ejaculation>>

The <<person1>><<person>> shoves you against the cabinet, before wandering off.
<br><br>

<<tearful>> you gather yourself.
<br><br>

<<clotheson>>
<<endcombat>>
/*
$logprep should be "..., when I was done" or "...I kept playing despite a "+$person+" moving to stand very close to me and then"
*/
<<set $logprep to $logprep+" "+$he+" "+$aw_xedx+" until "+$he+" was satisfied.">>
<<log $logprep 3>>
<<endevent $eventstr>>

<<link [[Next|Arcade]]>><</link>>

<<elseif $enemyhealth lte 0>>

You shove the <<person>> to the ground.
<br><br>

<<tearful>> you take cover beneath a pinball machine.
<br><br>

<<clotheson>>
<<endcombat>>
<<set $logprep to $logprep+" "+$he+" started to "+$aw_xx+" but I managed to shove "+$him+" away before "+$he+" was finished.">>
<<log $logprep 3>>
<<endevent $eventstr>>

<<link [[Next|Arcade]]>><</link>>

<<else>>
<<set $rescued += 1>>

Your cry attracts attention. People look over, including a member of staff. The <<person1>><<person>> steps away from you, claiming that <<he>> wasn't doing anything. <<He>> doesn't try anything else.
<br><br>

<<tearful>> you gather yourself.
<br><br>

<<clotheson>>
<<endcombat>>
<<set $logprep to $logprep+" "+$he+" started to "+$aw_xx+" but I managed to cry out and attract attention of other people before "+$he+" was finished.">>
<<log $logprep 3>>
<<endevent $eventstr>>

<<link [[Next|Arcade]]>><</link>>

<</if>>

:: Arcade Watched Shove [nobr]
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "town">><<effects>>

You manage to shove the <<person>> away.
<br><br>
<<He>> decides to leave when people start looking in your direction. 
<<log $logprep 2>>

<<endevent $eventstr>>

<<link [[Next|Arcade]]>><</link>>

